1
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:11,257
The spines that this mask
uses can pierce a human brain.

2
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:16,177
However, they don't yet have the
strength to probe our immortal brains.

3
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:18,920
The solution is finding more power.

4
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:27,477
Ooh, what's that now?

5
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:30,031
The mortals call it the Red Stone of Asia.

6
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:33,320
Its power is of a particular
interest for our kind.

7
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:37,548
This little stone can refract
light at least a billion times.

8
00:00:37,940 --> 00:00:41,352
The end result is light of
incredible purity and strength.

9
00:00:41,960 --> 00:00:44,980
This amplified light holds power untold.

10
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:47,260
But this one won't do.

11
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:50,080
This little red pebble isn't large enough.

12
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:52,877
We need more capacity and strength in it.

13
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:58,040
To complete our mask, we need a red
stone that is large and utterly flawless.

14
00:00:58,580 --> 00:01:00,980
We need a super Asia.

15
00:01:01,540 --> 00:01:02,780
Once we have that,

16
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:09,200
we will conquer the sun and then become
the final perfect step in evolution.

17
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:19,240
The masks were invented by the oldest
pillar man among them, and his name is Kars.

18
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:25,880
Cars ACDC and Mama cross the Atlantic in
their search for a suitable Super Asia.

19
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:27,573
There you are, Susie Q.

20
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:30,460
Signora, here, just like you wanted.

21
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:31,700
Thank you.

22
00:01:32,460 --> 00:01:33,640
You see this?

23
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:37,980
What I have in my hand here is a
natural, perfectly flawless stone.

24
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:40,460
A Super Asia. Whoa!

25
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:44,901
You've been carrying the
red stone of Asia around?

26
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:55,200
The warriors of Harmon were
wiped out by the Pillar Men.

27
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:58,080
This stone narrowly avoided being taken,

28
00:01:58,340 --> 00:02:01,575
and now I have been given
the honor to be its guardian.

29
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:06,620
Caesar, I know exactly how you feel.

30
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:10,780
The stone masks not only
killed our grandfathers,

31
00:02:10,980 --> 00:02:14,039
but they took the lives of
countless others as well.

32
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:17,100
And now we've met its creator, Kars.

33
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:18,600
Just break it!

34
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,940
Yeah, crush the damn thing.

35
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:24,180
Smash it to pieces and
they'll cry like babies.

36
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:26,220
No, I can't do that. Why?

37
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:27,397
What's stopping you?

38
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:29,417
Legend says the Pillamen can't be defeated

39
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:33,960
unless the stone is somehow a part
of the process. What? That's crazy.

40
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:35,279
Why would that be?

41
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:36,420
I don't know.

42
00:02:37,580 --> 00:02:41,540
But I will perform my duty
as guardian as best I can.

43
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:48,240
Jojo, Caesar, I'm afraid it's
necessary for a final examination.

44
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:50,070
What?

45
00:02:50,153 --> 00:02:50,983
A final exam?

46
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:53,520
Caesar, take on Machina and defeat him.

47
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:56,877
Jojo, you have the same
assignment but with logs.

48
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:58,019
Are you two ready?

49
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:30,600
Thank you.

50
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:02,120
Thank you.

51
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:37,140
Are you ready, Caesar?

52
00:04:37,460 --> 00:04:38,640
I was born ready!

53
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:49,200
It's almost dawn.

54
00:04:50,180 --> 00:04:52,060
It's always darkest then.

55
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:55,740
Now, where could I
expect Logs to be hiding?

56
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:58,940
Stay sharp, Joseph. Eyes open.

57
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:01,475
You've got a score to settle with him.

58
00:05:02,660 --> 00:05:03,490
Huh?

59
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:06,560
Is that Instructor Logs?

60
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:10,500
Horrible! Unnatural!

61
00:05:11,700 --> 00:05:12,840
Instructor Logs!

62
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:15,180
He's dead!

63
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:20,600
Easy Pass!

64
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:22,800
So you came to Venice!

65
00:05:23,140 --> 00:05:24,611
Came here to this island!

66
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:37,560
To think that the woman guarding the stone
is merely an island or two over that way.

67
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:46,040
His lungs were pulled out.

68
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,020
Lungs are vital for Harmon users.

69
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:53,005
It had to have been a
kick of incredible power.

70
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:55,777
The tyrant logs.

71
00:05:55,860 --> 00:05:58,600
You yelled at me for three weeks.

72
00:05:59,520 --> 00:06:01,697
You were relentless
with your instructions.

73
00:06:01,780 --> 00:06:04,040
To be honest, I hated you.

74
00:06:04,740 --> 00:06:09,697
I was sure that this would be my chance to
get you back for everything you did to me

75
00:06:09,780 --> 00:06:12,477
you'll have to watch me from where you are

76
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:16,200
now instructor see what
i've learned from you

77
00:06:23,780 --> 00:06:28,157
hey acedisi i know it's
six days early but i'll

78
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:32,700
take it now that antidote
in your nose ring is mine

79
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:38,297
out of my way boy i don't
have the time to deal

80
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:40,637
with you you don't have
the time what do you

81
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:46,217
mean you have a lot more
time than i do that was

82
00:06:46,300 --> 00:06:49,124
pretty sharp you may have
a little more to offer

83
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:53,959
but when someone looks at me with
an obvious challenge like that one?

84
00:06:54,700 --> 00:06:56,760
They are asking for their death.

85
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:04,380
I'll tell you this one
more time. Back away.

86
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:09,077
You know that with one touch of my hand,
you'll soon be missing half of your body.

87
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:10,520
Just try to move me.

88
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:16,450
Ooh.

89
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:19,020
What's this now? Oh, look.

90
00:07:19,140 --> 00:07:20,200
I'm still here.

91
00:07:20,420 --> 00:07:23,832
I only move for important
things, like dog poo in my path.

92
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:30,136
Using his hamon, he's able to break
right through the flesh of my hand.

93
00:07:30,260 --> 00:07:34,260
He's learned a great deal of control
in a very short period of time.

94
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:36,590
However...

95
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:43,947
You've developed new skills.

96
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:46,139
I have to say I'm rather surprised.

97
00:07:48,220 --> 00:07:51,417
But you're still far from
ready to fight someone like me!

98
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:56,500
I've met and devoured countless Hamon
users like you thousands of years ago!

99
00:07:57,920 --> 00:08:03,120
If I twist your finger completely off,
you'll never use it for Hamon ever again!

100
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:05,600
Like this!

101
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:11,200
Oh, you finally noticed!

102
00:08:11,580 --> 00:08:15,040
Your arm is wrapped up in
a loop of fine silk thread.

103
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:19,997
It's soaked in vegetable oil, so it
really conducts Hamon quite well.

104
00:08:20,080 --> 00:08:24,517
I admit I was aiming for your neck,
but you didn't give me the chance.

105
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:27,440
How could a mortal have done this to me?

106
00:08:30,860 --> 00:08:32,520
But but that's.

107
00:08:33,400 --> 00:08:35,757
Actually a little morbid for my taste,

108
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:40,660
but still first blood goes
to me and my instructor. Ah!

109
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:50,720
2,500 years ago in China,
a man wrote The Art of War.

110
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:57,020
He said this, victory is decided
before the battle is fought.

111
00:08:58,200 --> 00:09:00,420
That means if you plan to win,

112
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:04,287
you need to lay out strategies
while your opponent is unaware.

113
00:09:04,380 --> 00:09:06,637
It's true that I skipped school a lot,

114
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:10,320
But Granny Iran made darn
sure I studied my history.

115
00:09:11,220 --> 00:09:13,957
So while you may have a lot
of years under your belt,

116
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:17,099
you didn't leave any room
in your head for strategy.

117
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:20,220
Take that!

118
00:09:29,460 --> 00:09:30,640
How dare you?

119
00:09:30,980 --> 00:09:32,400
Oh, are you angry?

120
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:35,681
Are you upset that I
disintegrated your widow arm?

121
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:38,014
Well, then, get upset!

122
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:40,020
I'm far more furious than you!

123
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:43,517
Because of that little ring you
saw fit to put inside my neck,

124
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:45,482
I haven't slept right for weeks!

125
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:47,910
Huh?

126
00:09:50,580 --> 00:09:53,040
I just can't take it!

127
00:09:54,220 --> 00:09:55,050
No! No!

128
00:09:57,840 --> 00:10:01,337
I just can't take it!

129
00:10:01,420 --> 00:10:02,577
What the hell is this?

130
00:10:02,660 --> 00:10:06,820
He's bawling his eyes out, and I
thought he'd go on a bloody rampage.

131
00:10:07,140 --> 00:10:08,840
This is more than weird.

132
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:10,420
This is embarrassing.

133
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:13,722
He's throwing a tantrum
like some three-year-old.

134
00:10:19,300 --> 00:10:21,120
My poor arm!

135
00:10:24,780 --> 00:10:27,427
Some things are creepier
than mindless anger.

136
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:30,200
I should finish him off quickly.

137
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:48,680
I feel better now.

138
00:10:49,160 --> 00:10:51,520
Sometimes my emotions overwhelm me.

139
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:53,317
And when I'm about to lose it,

140
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:56,635
I try to calm myself down by
venting with a crying jag.

141
00:10:58,080 --> 00:11:00,700
Earlier you referred
to Sun Tzu, didn't you?

142
00:11:01,560 --> 00:11:03,320
I knew him personally.

143
00:11:03,740 --> 00:11:06,540
Long ago, I journeyed to China to study.

144
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:09,120
To fight us to delude.

145
00:11:09,520 --> 00:11:10,755
All war is deception.

146
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:13,617
One tries to make their
enemies angry in order

147
00:11:13,700 --> 00:11:16,347
to lure them into
committing costly mistakes.

148
00:11:16,460 --> 00:11:19,257
That is precisely what you're
planning on, am I right?

149
00:11:19,340 --> 00:11:21,046
Well, it's not going to work.

150
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:25,120
But I must say, Jojo, I really
am shocked at your improvement.

151
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:28,300
I admire your harm-on ability.

152
00:11:29,180 --> 00:11:31,560
I've been longing for a worthy opponent.

153
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:34,340
What the hell?

154
00:11:34,540 --> 00:11:35,658
What are you doing?

155
00:11:37,940 --> 00:11:39,897
Well, it is a bit thin at the moment,

156
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:42,804
but it'll grow thicker
with the passage of time.

157
00:11:44,760 --> 00:11:45,997
He's too much.

158
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:48,100
Just a minute ago, he was crying.

159
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:49,500
Oh, Jojo.

160
00:11:49,900 --> 00:11:51,665
Did I just frighten you there?

161
00:11:51,800 --> 00:11:52,997
Come on, admit it.

162
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:54,277
You're frightened a lot, aren't you?

163
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:56,600
I can't read him.

164
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,297
I've always been able to read my opponents

165
00:11:59,380 --> 00:12:02,027
and then use their own
feelings against them.

166
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:05,400
But this guy's personality is beyond me.

167
00:12:06,020 --> 00:12:08,079
Am I the one who's being read here?

168
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:14,260
What's happening to Log's body?

169
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:19,940
That burns!

170
00:12:20,300 --> 00:12:22,580
His body, it's boiling.

171
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:24,660
What's going on?

172
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:28,157
An animal's core temperature
will increase when

173
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:31,122
its fighting disease are
greatly exerting itself.

174
00:12:31,380 --> 00:12:35,480
I can raise my blood up to 500
degrees and then shoot it out at will.

175
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:37,717
At the same time, I took off his arm.

176
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:40,940
I also sent in some of my
boiling blood to show you.

177
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:45,320
With his divine sandstorm,
Wamu can control the wind.

178
00:12:45,940 --> 00:12:48,240
My domain is that of heat.

179
00:12:48,720 --> 00:12:50,780
I control the inferno.

180
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:56,200
I'll grant that your power to destroy
a defenseless, dead body is amazing.

181
00:12:56,820 --> 00:13:00,938
But I can also see that the reason
you did it was to try and scare me!

182
00:13:01,980 --> 00:13:04,040
Now try a clack of volley!

183
00:13:04,780 --> 00:13:07,520
My hormone isn't like it was a month ago!

184
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:12,960
I really did frighten you.

185
00:13:13,900 --> 00:13:15,037
You see, Jojo,

186
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:19,660
your uncontrolled emotions caused you
to attack me recklessly and too soon.

187
00:13:20,780 --> 00:13:23,817
My veins will inject boiling
blood into your skull

188
00:13:23,900 --> 00:13:27,780
and then turn your brain
into a nice red stew.

189
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:32,620
This is the reason that I am
called the Burning King! Gah!

190
00:13:33,340 --> 00:13:34,170
Gah!

191
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:38,280
Gah! Gah! Gah! Gah!

192
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:40,150
Gah!

193
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:43,350
Gah!

194
00:13:50,660 --> 00:13:52,000
SEASUR, TAKE THIS!

195
00:13:52,860 --> 00:13:53,690
ABOLUNCHE!

196
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:00,750
SEASUR, STOP!

197
00:14:00,900 --> 00:14:01,900
Hold your attack!

198
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:06,560
If we continue this contest,
one or both of us will die.

199
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:10,820
And much as my ego doesn't want
to admit it, I'd be the loser.

200
00:14:11,380 --> 00:14:15,237
For nearly ten years more than
you, I've been in preparation here.

201
00:14:15,320 --> 00:14:18,060
But today, your hormone
attack was so focused,

202
00:14:18,220 --> 00:14:20,867
you were able to burn
the hair off of my arm.

203
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:24,440
What else can I do after
being shamed like this?

204
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:28,740
You have passed your final
exam with flying colors.

205
00:14:41,300 --> 00:14:43,677
You should feel a sense of pride for this.

206
00:14:43,760 --> 00:14:48,017
Or are you more interested in how your
good-for-nothing friend is doing in his exam,

207
00:14:48,100 --> 00:14:48,930
Caesar?

208
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:53,257
The only reason I had
the power I did in this

209
00:14:53,340 --> 00:14:56,620
training is that I wanted
to match Jojo's talents.

210
00:14:57,240 --> 00:15:01,800
In the end, we're both going to survive
the trials being presented to us.

211
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:03,480
I can't deny it.

212
00:15:03,700 --> 00:15:05,700
Jojo seems lazy and impudent.

213
00:15:06,460 --> 00:15:09,107
But deep down, he's
worth having as a friend.

214
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,897
You're not so good at making
friends for yourself, are you?

215
00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:15,451
But when you do, it's true love, isn't it?

216
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:17,600
Look there!

217
00:15:19,520 --> 00:15:20,360
It's in easy!

218
00:15:21,380 --> 00:15:22,210
Hmm.

219
00:15:22,293 --> 00:15:24,777
And there's another of those
clever dodges of yours.

220
00:15:24,860 --> 00:15:25,690
All right.

221
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:28,920
The mask gave me some
protection that time, but...

222
00:15:36,140 --> 00:15:37,780
Ah, damn him and his blood!

223
00:15:42,180 --> 00:15:43,300
Man, oh man,

224
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:45,357
I finally have the chance for these sexy

225
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:47,637
lips to come out from
under that rotten mask.

226
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:51,132
And the first thing you do,
you bastard, is burn them off!

227
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:53,797
Jojo, hmm, let's see.

228
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:56,017
On the surface you make witty banter.

229
00:15:56,100 --> 00:16:00,160
But inside your head you're making
all sorts of plans, aren't you?

230
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:04,420
You went pale, Jojo Did I hit the mark?

231
00:16:04,580 --> 00:16:07,240
Was I anywhere close to the bullseye?

232
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:14,280
My next plan...

233
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:17,920
Right, yes, I'll use the string.

234
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:20,797
I'll act like I'm dodging
to get away from him,

235
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:25,137
but all the time I'll be running a string
along these spikes with each move I make.

236
00:16:25,220 --> 00:16:26,760
I can't let him catch on.

237
00:16:27,020 --> 00:16:28,897
Once he steps inside the string,

238
00:16:28,980 --> 00:16:32,627
I'll wrap him up in it, then use
my hormone to finish him off.

239
00:16:40,020 --> 00:16:41,980
That laugh means trouble.

240
00:16:42,860 --> 00:16:44,760
Could he be reading my plan?

241
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:45,760
My intentions?

242
00:16:46,900 --> 00:16:48,500
No, it's impossible.

243
00:16:58,760 --> 00:17:01,420
Here is the Burning King's prison!

244
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:07,960
How long can you possibly keep
avoiding my attacks, Jojo?

245
00:17:10,820 --> 00:17:12,880
So I guess you finally noticed.

246
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:16,240
Now what possible reason
would my hat be shrieking?

247
00:17:16,800 --> 00:17:18,880
You appear to be caught in my well.

248
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:22,660
My hat is made of 100 % wool.

249
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:24,666
It conducts harmon very well.

250
00:17:25,680 --> 00:17:26,510
And...

251
00:17:26,593 --> 00:17:27,717
You're smiling again.

252
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:28,717
I don't like it.

253
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:30,637
What are you laughing about this time?

254
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:32,557
The next words from your mouth are,

